  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-05T20:06:54.032Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the advent of the eye tracking starting to be implemented into VRChat more natively, this opens up the question as to what else on an avatar that could possibly be controlled via face tracking, and that leads to Visemes. Currently visemes on an avatar control animations on an avatar by 'selecting' a viseme index (at least as far as they are implemented on the animator). There is currently no way to control these as they are not networked or endpointed in any way.\n\nIt would be really awesome to have either the viseme index or the ability to send a float to each index to indicate the intensity of the viseme. This would allow apps such as VRCFaceTracking to emulate face tracking via visemes using built-in data transformers.\n\nThis would open the door for avatars to have more support for face tracking, and I believe this is an obvious and first step in introducing face tracking gradually, whilst also keeping backwards compatibility with existing avatars.\n\nPlease consider adding the ability for OSC to control visemes in some way.",
